        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Shallow ReLUs Networks in Lp-Type and Sobolev Spaces</title>\n    <script>\n        MathJax = {\n            tex: {\n                inlineMath: [['$', '$'], ['\\\\(', '\\\\)']],\n                displayMath: [['$$', '$$'], ['\\\\[', '\\\\]']],\n                packages: {'[+]': ['mathscr']}\n            },\n            svg: {\n                fontCache: 'global'\n            }\n        };\n    </script>\n    <script id=\"MathJax-script\" async src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js\"></script>\n    <style>\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Latin Modern Roman', 'Computer Modern Roman', 'Times New Roman', Times, serif;\n            font-size: 16px;\n            line-height: 1.4;\n            color: #000;\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            background-color: #fff;\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: center;\n        }\n        .page {\n            width: 850px;\n            min-height: 1100px;\n            padding: 80px 100px 80px 120px;\n            position: relative;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n            background: #fff;\n        }\n        .watermark {\n            position: absolute;\n            left: 30px;\n            top: 50%;\n            transform: translateY(-50%) rotate(-90deg);\n            color: #555;\n            font-size: 15px;\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n            white-space: nowrap;\n            letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n        }\n        .title {\n            text-align: center;\n            font-size: 1.35em;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 40px;\n            line-height: 1.3;\n        }\n        .author-section {\n            margin-bottom: 50px;\n        }\n        .author-block {\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: flex-start;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n        .author-info {\n            flex: 1;\n        }\n        .author-name {\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 2px;\n            font-size: 1.05em;\n        }\n        .author-affil {\n            font-style: italic;\n            font-size: 0.95em;\n            line-height: 1.25;\n        }\n        .author-email {\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            letter-spacing: 0.5px;\n            margin-top: 2px;\n        }\n        .abstract-container {\n            margin: 0 40px 40px 40px;\n        }\n        .abstract-title {\n            text-align: center;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            font-size: 1.15em;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n        }\n        .abstract-text {\n            text-align: justify;\n            font-size: 0.95em;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n            text-indent: 1.5em;\n        }\n        .keywords {\n            text-align: justify;\n            font-size: 0.95em;\n            margin-top: 10px;\n        }\n        h1 {\n            font-size: 1.15em;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-top: 40px;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            text-align: left;\n        }\n        p {\n            text-align: justify;\n            margin-top: 0;\n            margin-bottom: 1em;\n            text-indent: 1.5em;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n        }\n        p.noindent {\n            text-indent: 0;\n        }\n        .footnote-container {\n            margin-top: 60px;\n        }\n        .footnote-rule {\n            width: 150px;\n            border-top: 0.5px solid #000;\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n        }\n        .footnote-text {\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            line-height: 1.3;\n            text-align: left;\n        }\n        .page-number {\n            text-align: center;\n            margin-top: 50px;\n            font-size: 1em;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"page\">\n        <div class=\"watermark\">arXiv:2605.18468v1 [stat.ML] 18 May 2026</div>\n\n        <div class=\"title\">\n            Shallow ReLU$^s$ Networks in $L^p$-Type and Sobolev Spaces:<br>\n            Approximation and Path-Norm Controlled Generalization$^*$\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"author-section\">\n            <div class=\"author-block\">\n                <div class=\"author-info\">\n                    <div class=\"author-name\">Weizhao Li</div>\n                    <div class=\"author-affil\">\n                        School of Mathematical Sciences<br>\n                        Fudan University<br>\n                        Shanghai, China\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"author-email\">WEIZHAOLI24@M.FUDAN.EDU.CN</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"author-block\">\n                <div class=\"author-info\">\n                    <div class=\"author-name\">Fanghui Liu</div>\n                    <div class=\"author-affil\">\n                        School of Mathematical Sciences<br>\n                        Institute of Natural Sciences and MOE-LSC<br>\n                        Shanghai Jiao Tong University<br>\n                        Shanghai, China\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"author-email\">FANGHUI.LIU@SJTU.EDU.CN</div>\n            </div>\n\n            <div class=\"author-block\">\n                <div class=\"author-info\">\n                    <div class=\"author-name\">Lei Shi</div>\n                    <div class=\"author-affil\">\n                        School of Mathematical Sciences<br>\n                        Shanghai Key Laboratory for Contemporary Applied Mathematics<br>\n                        Fudan University<br>\n                        Shanghai, China\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"author-email\">LEISHI@FUDAN.EDU.CN</div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"abstract-container\">\n            <div class=\"abstract-title\">Abstract</div>\n            <div class=\"abstract-text\">\n                We study approximation by shallow ReLU$^s$ networks, $\\sigma_s(t) = \\max\\{0,t\\}^s$, and the generalization behavior of such networks under $\\ell_1$ path-norm control. For the $L^p$-type integral spaces $\\widetilde{\\mathcal{F}}_{p,\\tau_d,s}$, $1 \\le p \\le 2$, we prove approximation bounds for shallow networks using spherical harmonic analysis. In particular, when the parameter measure is the uniform measure $\\tau_d$ and $p < p^* = \\frac{2d+2}{d+3}$, we obtain the rate $O\\Big(m^{-\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{d(2-p)}{2d(2-p)+2p(2s+d+1)}} \\log^{\\frac{3}{2}} m\\Big)$, which improves the corresponding random-feature rate. We also derive approximation rates for Sobolev spaces $W^{\\alpha,p}$ in the range $1 \\le p < 2$ by embedding them into spectral Barron spaces. Finally, for nonparametric regression with sub-Gaussian noise, we prove minimax-optimal generalization bounds for path-norm-regularized shallow ReLU$^s$ networks: the rates are $O\\Big(n^{-\\frac{d+2s+1}{2d+2s+1}}\\log n\\Big)$ over $\\mathscr{B}_s$ and $O\\Big(n^{-\\frac{2\\alpha}{2\\alpha+d}}\\log n\\Big)$ over $W^{\\alpha,\\infty}$, with matching lower bounds up to logarithmic factors.\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"keywords\">\n                <strong>Keywords:</strong> Neural Networks, Sobolev Spaces, Variation Spaces, Path Norm\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <h1>1 Introduction</h1>\n        <p class=\"noindent\">\n            Deep learning has shown remarkable effectiveness in high-dimensional approximation problems, particularly in scientific computing, inverse problems, and operator learning (Han et al., 2018; Adcock et al., 2022; Beck et al., 2023). In many such settings, the ReLU$^s$ activation $\\sigma_s(t) = \\max\\{0, t\\}^s$ ($s \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$) is especially relevant because it yields piecewise-polynomial representations that are well suited to smooth targets and derivative-sensitive tasks (Yang and Zhou, 2025; He et al., 2024).\n        </p>\n\n        <div class=\"footnote-container\">\n            <div class=\"footnote-rule\"></div>\n            <div class=\"footnote-text\">\n                *. Authors are listed in alphabetical order and contributed equally to this work. Corresponding authors:<br>\n                Fanghui Liu and Lei Shi.\n            </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"page-number\">1</div>\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>"
